# Italy Legal Entry — .gitignore
# Nothing generated, nothing local, nothing secret. Every pattern was checked against
# `git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard` (it must stay empty): no tracked file is hidden by this file.

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
/env/

# ---- Tool caches ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/

# ---- Coverage and test outputs ----------------------------------------------------------------
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/
junit*.xml

# ---- Playwright artefacts (browser tests and the QA scripts) -----------------------------------
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
traces/
*.trace.zip

# ---- Django: collected static, uploads, private documents, local databases, logs ---------------
/staticfiles/
/media/
/private_media/
# config/settings/test.py writes its media under ./tmp
/tmp/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite
*.sql
*.dump
*.log
logs/

# ---- Environment and secrets: the example file is the only one that belongs in the repository --
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ---- Node / frontend tooling -------------------------------------------------------------------
# static/js/dist and static/css/dist ARE versioned: the host runs collectstatic, not Node.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/
# esbuild sourcemaps are written only by `npm run watch:js` / `watch:css` and never shipped
static/js/dist/**/*.map
static/css/dist/**/*.map

# ---- OS and editors ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# Office lock files (a document left open next to the repository)
~$*
.~lock.*#
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp

# ---- Local agent / session state — never part of the project ----------------------------------
.remember/
.claude/*.local.json

# ---- Local screenshots and capture folders (QA runs, design reviews): regenerated, not versioned
# `screenshots/` is anchored on purpose: docs/audit/current-site/screenshots/ is tracked evidence.
shots/
/screenshots/
/captures/
docs/qa/**/*.png
docs/qa/**/*.jpeg
!docs/qa/golden/**
# Direction prototypes: the self-check frame dumps stay on disk for the council, not in history
docs/design-v2/directions/*/shots/
docs/design-v2/council/shots/
# V3 audit captures: evidence for the report, regenerated by the QA scripts
docs/design-v3/audit/

# ---- Confidential source documents (docs/security/CONFIDENTIAL_MATERIAL_POLICY.md) -------------
# The 20 Sept 2026 package is an unpublished work pending SIAE deposit and the Mod. 350 carries
# personal data. It lives outside the repository; these patterns are a second line of defence.
*.docx
mod_350*
*RISERVATO*
docItaly*
docs/source-of-truth/_raw/
# No PDF is tracked (checked 8 Oct 2026) and the documents removed from history on 21 Sept 2026
# were PDFs. A public one, should there ever be one, is re-included explicitly with a `!` rule.
*.pdf

# The two 17 Sept 2026 documents of the client and their full-text extractions. They WERE tracked
# under docs/source/ and were removed from the working tree and from every commit on 21 Sept 2026:
# a PDF belonging to the client, with its author and its internal instructions, is not a public
# artefact merely because some of its sentences end up on a page. The originals live next to the
# other source material outside the repository; scripts/verify_locked_against_source.py reads them
# from there through ILE_SOURCE_DIR. See docs/security/HISTORY_REWRITE_2026-09-21.md.
docs/source/
ILE_Document_Implementation_FR.*
ILE_Annexe_1_Textes_Juridiques_FR.*
